# TypeScript Quality

- Strict TypeScript; avoid `any` and `unknown`
- Keep files small and composable
- Do not refactor unless requested
- Shared types go in `src/lib/types`
- Local-only types can stay in file
- Prefer descriptive handler names (e.g. `handleSubmit`)
- Constants and enums use `ALL_CAPS`

## Naming Rules
- Folders: `kebab-case`
- Folder names use lowercase words separated by hyphens
- `.ts` (non-components): `camelCase`
- `.tsx` components: `PascalCase`
- Classes (if used): `PascalCase`
- No snake_case
- No kebab-case for files
- No PascalCase for non-class `.ts` files
